# Database checks

These scripts test the SQL functions, row-level security and concurrency of the self-hosted database. They read `SUPABASE_DB_URL` and the Supabase keys from `.env` (written by `npm

## Migrations and regressions

```sh
node supabase/tests/migrations.mjs
```

Replays every migration into a temporary schema, compares it with the current schema (columns, constraints, indexes, RLS, policies, views, triggers, functions), and runs the `.sql`

`workspace-isolation.sql` seeds two synthetic users with records in every application table and checks, as the `authenticated` role, that neither can see or change the other's data

Single regressions run with their `run-*.mjs` script, for example `node supabase/tests/run-goal-reservations.mjs`. `run-sql.mjs` runs the import-review fixture.

## Concurrency

`*-concurrency.mjs` scripts (chat, imports, reviews, recurring occurrences, reservations) open separate authenticated and service connections to check locks, cancellation and dupli

